{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0176UF286B32dUZGptgDMN1U","type":"tool_result","content":"                <h2>📖 Plot Summary</h2>\n                <div style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; white-space: pre-wrap;\">Mrs. Sigourney Howard, a reflective and observant woman, recounts her experiences in the summer of 1922, set against the glittering yet hollow backdrop of Long Island’s East and West Egg. She begins her story with her arrival in West Egg, where she rents a modest home and quickly becomes entangled in the lives of her cousin Daisy Buchanan and her domineering husband Tom, a man whose racist rhetoric and emotional cruelty unsettle her. Her introduction to the enigmatic Jay Gatsby occurs on a fateful night when she sees him standing on the lawn, arms outstretched toward a distant green light across the bay—a symbol of his unattainable dream. This moment marks the beginning of her deepening involvement with Gatsby, whose lavish parties and mysterious past intrigue her, even as she remains wary of the illusions he cultivates.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6595f10d-dd12-40e9-9d88-7f5d63eb6af8","uuid":"8498ed34-470b-432b-b15a-b00c86c1351e","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"                <h2>📖 Plot Summary</h2>\n                <div style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; white-space: pre-wrap;\">Mrs. Sigourney Howard, a reflective and observant woman, recounts her experiences in the summer of 1922, set against the glittering yet hollow backdrop of Long Island’s East and West Egg. She begins her story with her arrival in West Egg, where she rents a modest home and quickly becomes entangled in the lives of her cousin Daisy Buchanan and her domineering husband Tom, a man whose racist rhetoric and emotional cruelty unsettle her. Her introduction to the enigmatic Jay Gatsby occurs on a fateful night when she sees him standing on the lawn, arms outstretched toward a distant green light across the bay—a symbol of his unattainable dream. This moment marks the beginning of her deepening involvement with Gatsby, whose lavish parties and mysterious past intrigue her, even as she remains wary of the illusions he cultivates.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false}}
